Approach

Roman numerals are formed by converting each decimal place (thousands, hundreds, tens, and ones) separately and concatenating the results from left to right.

Algorithm
We use four String[] arrays to store the Roman numeral representations for:
Thousands (M)
Hundreds (C)
Tens (X)
Ones (I)
Each array stores all possible values for its place:
M : 0 - 3000
C : 0 - 900
X : 0 - 90
I : 0 - 9

The number is decomposed into its place values using integer division and modulo operations:

M[num / 1000]
+ C[(num % 1000) / 100]
+ X[(num % 100) / 10]
+ I[num % 10]

Each index directly maps to its Roman numeral representation, eliminating the need for loops, conditionals, or HashMaps. The final answer is obtained by concatenating the four strings.

Complexity
Time Complexity: O(1)
Space Complexity: O(1)